        }
      ],
      "solution": "$y = x^2\\sqrt{x^2 + 2x} = x^2(x^2 + 2x)^{\\frac{1}{2}}$\n$\\therefore \\frac{dy}{dx} = 2x(x^2 + 2x)^{\\frac{1}{2}} + x^2 \\times \\frac{1}{2}(x^2 + 2x)^{-\\frac{1}{2}}(2x + 2) \\quad \\{\\text{product rule}\\}\n= 2x\\sqrt{x^2 + 2x} + \\frac{x^2(x + 1)}{\\sqrt{x^2 + 2x}}$",
      "ai_explanation": {
        "concept_rule": "Product rule: $(uv)' = u'v + uv'$, where one factor requires the chain rule.",
        "step_by_step": [
          "Let $u = x^2$ and $v = (x^2 + 2x)^{1/2}$.",
          "Find $u' = 2x$ and $v' = \\frac{1}{2}(x^2 + 2x)^{-1/2}(2x + 2) = \\frac{x + 1}{\\sqrt{x^2 + 2x}}$.",
          "Combine terms using the product rule: $2x\\sqrt{x^2 + 2x} + \\frac{x^2(x + 1)}{\\sqrt{x^2 + 2x}}$."
        ],
        "common_pitfalls": "Forgetting to differentiate the inner expression $2x + 2$ when applying the chain rule to the radical."
      }
    },
    {
