      ],
      "solution": "$y = \\sqrt{x}(2x + 3)^4 = x^{\\frac{1}{2}}(2x + 3)^4$\n$\\therefore \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{1}{2}x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}(2x + 3)^4 + x^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\times 4(2x + 3)^3(2) \\quad \\{\\text{product rule}\\}\n= \\frac{(2x + 3)^4}{2\\sqrt{x}} + 8\\sqrt{x}(2x + 3)^3$",
      "ai_explanation": {
